A||||72||Eric||fart fart fart fart||||12||
Z||000000||Eric||02-16-2001||02:54 PM||||I think I had a challenge from a Del Sol today.  The guy was beside me in the left turn lane and just a little behind when I heard the unmistakable farting noise of rice being cooked in a coffee can muffler.  I wrenched my head around to get a look at my competition.  Of course the red car had 18 inch rims, stickers like VTEC and MUGEN all over the damn place, and a yellow interior!  The kid pulled up a little and reved his little tin can motor so I could read his intentions.  Well, his intentions weren't exactly clear.  First of all, he was in the turn lane and I wasn't.  Secondly, he gave me "the look".  I don't know exactly what the "I'm gonna race you and try to kick your ass" look looks like, but the look he gave included a fruity little smile and a wink.  I'm not sure the guy was gay, but what do you expect from someone who drives a Del Sol with a yellow interior.  Anyway, he turned left just like a good little boy, and left me back at the light.  God, that was strange.||||reg||12
Z||000001||p4n1c||02-16-2001||03:25 PM||||Oh no, don't race a fart can.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Sh** man, my parents cutlass with the 2.8 can beat one of those damn things.  New cars make me sad.  They are getting so horrible.  And people that think Honda's are reliable.  Walking to work today I hear a huge grinding noise, knocking and look over see a 96-97 Civic sedan(not hatchback) on the side of a 4 lane highway with it's 4 ways on and the hood up.  About 5 meters up, an 89-90 Honda or Toyota, couldn't tell with it's 4-ways on the side of the road with it's hood up.  Kinda tells you something.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)||||reg||1
Z||000002||loafer87gt||02-16-2001||03:50 PM||||Some of those little imports can be pretty quick. My bro has a 92 Civic SI with sticky Nitto tires on 16" wheels and the cars pulls really hard. The only mods he has is an akimoto intake and a cat back exhaust system. For a 1.6 litre engine, it moves pretty damn good, even giving my GT a scare a couple of times. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||RiceCooker||02-16-2001||04:21 PM||||that's too bad he turned<P>you woulda cooked em||||reg||6
Z||000004||Black88GT||02-16-2001||08:19 PM||||Vtec Del Sols would hand a stock Fiero its ass on a silver platter.  Check the stats on them.  However you don't see too many true Vtec Del Sols so it probably wasn't a real one.  My friend has a B16A motor in his CRX and it runs 13s, so next time you think its some ricer with a body kit, think twice because its becoming a popular swap with the Honduh guys....<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||02-16-2001||08:25 PM||||how can you tell if it's a v-tec or not? my friend says his civic has a 167hp v-tec. and his car just doesn't seem like it has that much horsepower. he can beat my 2.5, but that's not saying much. with nearly twice the hp as mine, i figured he could blow me away, but i can keep up with for a little bit.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sleeper||02-16-2001||10:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Vtec Del Sols would hand a stock Fiero its ass on a silver platter.  Check the stats on them.  However you don't see too many true Vtec Del Sols so it probably wasn't a real one.  My friend has a B16A motor in his CRX and it runs 13s, so next time you think its some ricer with a body kit, think twice because its becoming a popular swap with the Honduh guys...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>true that man,...i'm helping this dude at my work put a b16 in his 91 crx, it should run 13's like you said. they're doing the same thing we're doing putting bigger motors in their tiny cars.<BR><P>------------------<BR>85 GT<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels, Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering spring, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, Chris West's Strut Tower Bar, J.E.T. super chip, Accel Super Coil, Accel Wires, K&N filter and Optima Battery.||||reg||1
Z||000007||My7Fieros||02-16-2001||11:05 PM||||I like soy sauce on rice........<BR>Ive kicked MANY-a ricers a$$....let me say this to all of those "specs" people, the ONLY and I mean ONLY cars to ever "hand my Fiero its a$$ on a platter" was a 2000 Ram Air Trans Am and a 99/2000 Mustang GT...thats about as daring as I'll be when it comes to cars in that catagory.<BR>If you know how to drive, #'s dont mean sh1t!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Slammed Fiero||02-17-2001||12:29 AM||||My friends Vtec Del Slow Runs mid to high 15's , Never handed me my ass , its got a cold air intake , lowered and a wings west body kit. IT's not that fast. Hell the Type R's here are running borderline 14's , the fastest 2.8 I have heard of is running 15.3's.. The cars lack torque , I can smoke my friends Del sol from light to light , terrible weight transfer and traction.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Eric||02-17-2001||12:48 AM||||I honestly don't think this fruity little guy's car was a real VTEC.  The VTEC sticker on the rear bumper looked really cheesy, kinda like he added it on when he painted the interior yellow.  I know my car's not really fast, but I don't have any doubts about beating him to sixty or seventy, which is all the faster I'm willing to race on a public road.  Del Sols suck almost as much D as the people who drive them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Black88GT||02-17-2001||01:12 AM||||Well anytime you guys want to race my friends CRX with your 2.8's let me know when you'll be in town.  Actually, maybe I will bring him to Englishtown with me so he can humiliate any Fiero that shows up.  13s is with STREET TIRES.  Bring slicks and he runs high 12s.  Not trying to jock Honduh's but for around 5,000 bucks (including car) he is running 12s in his CRX.  I have put about that into mine and I would hope to run 14s.  Can't argue with facts.<P>So yeah keep thinking that your 2.8 can beat everything but brand new stangs and f-bodies.  Vtec Del Sols have 160 Hp and weigh around 2500 lbs.  I have "heard" that stock fieros run low-mid 15s, but I have yet to see this.  I trust magazines that show 16 second qtr. mile times for stock Fiero's, not "hearsay" that is commonly inaccurate.<BR>Hell, the new GMC SierraC3 is running qtr. mile better times then stock Fiero's.<P>Just the facts....||||reg||1
Z||000011||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||02-17-2001||03:13 AM||||a 13 second CRX is still a car that only children can fit in.  I had a 97 civic and I could not sit up straight in the car.<P>It broke a lot from the day I bought it.  It sounded like a boring car and it was. The handling was good but cornering power was a big weakness.  The body was built of tin foil and the interior fabric was garbage.  The door upholstery wore out in the first 5000 miles.  The crappy seats showed "butt wear" from the test drive forward.  The steering was clunky making bad noises on every bump the car encountered.  The dealership could not fix the problem telling me it "is not a mercedes"<P>On that point we agreed.  I traded a 1993 Z24 in for that Honda civic and it was a huge mistake.<P>So I say "Your friend can do the 1/4 in 13, but he still is driving a crappy honda."  Don't get me wrong, the accord and prelude are both very nice cars.  <P>The civics are absolute junk.  It's like saying "Dodge Neon can do 13 in the 1/4"  I still think it's a piece of **** .  <P>American cars are built for adults taller than 5'6" little Japanese cars are not.  No modification can change that.<P>Ever seen one of those ricermobiles with the Japanese writing on them?  Don't they look like some kind of christmas present?  Why would you want to make your car look like a gift?  And what is with those stupid flimsy 300lb wings that everybod has?  They suck from any perpective.<P>Sorry to rant, but when I see a rice mobile I think "an idiot owns that."  What the hell is a 5" muffler tip doing on a vehicle that is not made by Caterpillar, John Deere, or International Harvester?<P>Maybe honda means "farm equipment" in Japanese.  It certainly symbolizes a person lacking idividuality and creativity.  It depresses me to think that I bought one of those cars.  Just one, never again.||||reg||1
Z||000012||TheFiero64||02-17-2001||11:39 AM||||All those riced hondas with the fart cans make me LMAO.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000013||Black88GT||02-17-2001||04:40 PM||||Ummm FYI the CRX has much more cargo space then a Fiero does.  My sister has a CRX HF and it has plenty of room for me (5'10") and not to mention the seats are much more comfortable.<P>You talk about garbage interior and you have a Fiero?  Thats the Fiero's weakest part IMHO.  Seat tears are common, dash cracks on the vents are common, the center console and shift surround separate and curl, the seats sit too low where you feel like you are sitting on the ground, seats have little back support in comparison with Honda seats.<BR>The Fiero was trashed in every mag for ergonomics, one of the CRX's stonger points (ever been in one?  it has all kinds of neat little storage places). <P>Then you mention funny noises when you went over bumps, what about the Fiero's bump steer?I'm not sure if you drive that special Fiero but bumpsteer is another downside to Fiero's.  They cut it down in '88 but its still not that good.  <P>The Fiero is a great car but it has its faults.  Honda is known for its reliability durability, so to call it a "crappy" Honda is laughable.  Just because you had a lemon.  The ironic part is many people I have met that talk bad about Fiero's often owned an 84 or 85 2m4 model or just a Fiero that wasn't taken care of and they talk about how unreliable they were.  I try to explain that just because YOURS was bad doesnt mean ALL are bad.  It's the same thing in this case.<P>Most import guys that have nice engines don't have any stickers at all.  My friend doesn't have any on his CRX, just a body kit and big wheels.  The true ricers are NOT the people I am trying to defend, It's just annoying when any Honda is automatically "rice" no matter what.  I hate ricer mobiles as much as anyone but to call a 12 second Honda that can outperform and outhandle my car or your car is just plain senseless.<P>  <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Slammed Fiero||02-17-2001||07:38 PM||||Wow someone sure loves CRx's. For the amount of money it takes to make a CRX really fast you could do a lot more work to a fiero. It's a better platform for high Horsepower, more rigid chassis, mid engine cars are farrrr bettter for high HP applications (ever see a FWD indy car??).Get a Hi HP Front drive car and it's useful for one thing ..straight line ..thats it. The Weight transfer of a Hi po FWD car makes it useless for anything but straight line. <P><BR>As for the DEl Sol Vtec weighing in at 2500lbs ..Don't think so , Both SAE books I have here quote 2730 and 2810lbs. IF you interested in timeslips for a Stock fiero running low 15's go to<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/banditbalz</A> <BR>This is George Balzers page , 86 GT 4spd , low 15's.<P>I like Hondas, I had an 88 Civic , it handled well. I have a friend with a CRX , ZC16 Japenese spec motor , for you import junkies this is the same basically as the early 90's non Vtec integra motors (150hp) , twin cam. For what it cost him to have the motor put in professionally I could have built a basic V8 Fiero. The car is entertaining (his CRX) but it's not the bee all end all. YEah there are a lot of 13 sec honda's out there , but the majority of the kids around today have wanna be cars.<P>For a used Integra motor with VTEC along with the transmission your looking at 7 grand canadian. That is one of the best prices you will find anywhere. this is engine transmission and all related computer items. 40,000 Kms on it. I'm actually talking to my friend at Mach one Motorsports , his shop does lots of conversions. Even after the $10,000 install cost , the car is running mid to high 13's. This is a Very clean install with a header and a cat back exhaust. LSD Gear box , dyno tuned..ect..ect <P>Speaking from experience Hondas rust quite a bit , their parts are built to be very light and thus flex a lot. Fiero is over built , but feels more rugged than any civic I have ever ridden in. The door on my fiero feels like the door on my caddy (79 with a BB) ,if I were to have 400-500hp , this is a quality I would like to have.<P><BR>A 12 sec Civic would be hard pressed to out handle a shopping cart. Have you looked to see what they have to do to get the car into the 12's??? it usually has huge wheels on the front with rivited rims so the tire doesn't slip. Now how can that handle well.  The CRX I mentioned above ran 15.3's after the swap (ZC16) with a very good driver. it's a late CRX so it's heavier (2700lbs) He added a ZEX NOS kit (70hp shot) and it's running low 14's with slicks ..without them the car is useless. IT runs nearly a second slower..no traction at all. no room to put a big enough tire in. He runs Nitto Drag tires , on street he runs BFG G force Ta's<P>I see a lot of claims to 14, 13, 12 second civics and the kids that make the claim have no idea what it takes to make their car go that fast. I don't doubt your friend's car is a 13 sec car. But for the amount of money he put into it , i could get a C4 vette and run circles around any Honda for a lot less money<P>Their is always someone faster..I don't care what you drive.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Slammed Fiero||02-17-2001||07:50 PM||||A bit nieve to say your friends CRX will smoke any fiero...<P>Lets be serious ..a Northstar would beat him like a rented mule.<P>Chris moores N* car ran mid 13's in LIMP mode , limited to 70% total power to 45mph (according to lingenfeter) , it's at lingenfetler's shop now being tuned..night night Honda.<P>JM<P>Like I said ..there's always someone faster.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Sleeper||02-17-2001||10:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Wow someone sure loves CRx's. For the amount of money it takes to make a CRX really fast you could do a lot more work to a fiero. <P>For a used Integra motor with VTEC along with the transmission your looking at 7 grand canadian. That is one of the best prices you will find anywhere. this is engine transmission and all related computer items. 40,000 Kms on it. I'm actually talking to my friend at Mach one Motorsports , his shop does lots of conversions. Even after the $10,000 install cost , the car is running mid to high 13's. This is a Very clean install with a header and a cat back exhaust. LSD Gear box , dyno tuned..ect..ect <P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>hahahaha, jesus christ that was pretty funny, one of the most retarded things i've ever heard. your friends shop is full of sh*t.<P>around $500 for a running or rolling chassis CRX and then you run down to the junk or dismantling yard and get a good condition vtec motor and every thing for like 1 grand. so if you do everything yourself your getting a 13 sec car for like under 2 grand or $1500. take that sh*t to the bank.(i don't like hondas that much but the crx is the only one i'd buy because it's easy and cheap to get low 1/4 mile times.)<P><BR>Black88GT: my uncle lives out in Belcamp(i think it's near you) and he tells me the import scene has hit pretty hard there so i know what you mean about this crx thing. i live in L.A. so its probably worst off here, but anyways you don't have to waste your time sticking up for crx's here cuz look at these other dudes, look where they live...boonyville, usa. the import scene really hasn't made it to their city yet. they are are just racing the hondas(or other imports) with lots stickers, fart can and a maga ricer wing they aren't seeing or racing the ones with a built motor, turbo or jackson supercharger. so might as well just chill cuz they're just gonna cry "ricer, ricer, ricer".  <BR><P>------------------<BR>85 GT<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels, Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering spring, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, Chris West's Strut Tower Bar, J.E.T. super chip, Accel Super Coil, Accel Wires, K&N filter and Optima Battery.||||reg||1
Z||000017||crzyone||02-17-2001||10:52 PM||||Fiero, with all the different V-8 mods you can put into it has alot more HP and Torque potential than a front wheel drive Honda.  Add to that, a Fiero with these mods can still run a track and not be limited to straight line drag racing.  Fieros, in my opinion, are a well rounded sports car.<P><P>------------------<BR>86 GT fastback 4 speed<BR>85 sport coupe 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000018||crzyone||02-17-2001||10:57 PM||||Also, front wheel drive cars will NEVER be faster than rear wheel drive cars. Front wheel drive has poor traction off the line, and this has been said many times.  <P>I like Honda but only RWD Hondas.<P>------------------<BR>86 GT fastback 4 speed<BR>85 sport coupe 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000019||Black88GT||02-17-2001||11:26 PM||||My friend bought a '91 HF model (best due to the weight) for 1,000 bucks.  Bought a B16A motor with accessories for around 2,000.  Integra axles he needed were like 300 I think.  Add 1,000 labor from Mid-Atlantic Motorsports.  So I was mistaken, it wasn't 5,000 it was 5,300.  $10,000 install is hillarious.  The mods required to put a B16A in a CRX is about the same as putting a 3.4 in a Fiero with a 4 speed auto.<P>I would like to see a C4 vette in good shape sell for 5,300, or 6,300 or even 7,300 that could outhandle/outperform his CRX.    <P>BTW, the ZC motor sucks, its only 130 Hp last I checked (don't quote me on that but I am pretty sure, I'll have to look).  That was a trend for a while until they discovered the B16A will fit with minor mods.  Weight of his car with no driver and full tank of gas was around 2,400 lbs. I believe. <P>OK, Northstar Fiero, how much did he put into that.  My friend right now is talking to EIP tuning for a possible turbo kit.  Can we say, 11's?  Let me see a Fiero timeslip for 11's.  <P>Sleepr, it will be funny when the Import scene DOES hit where they live.  I used to think just like them, "oh Honda's suck no CRX can outrun my Fiero!" it took a couple whoopings to teach me a few things about these cars.  I would usually flag them into a parking lot and talk for a while about their car.  It always amazed me how they can do that with small motors and FWD. <P>Live and learn...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||crzyone||02-17-2001||11:47 PM||||An ol' 427AC Cobra with 450HP and next to no weight can't even do 11's.  How can you expect a small FWD car to go that fast?  The Cobra only managed to do 13's like most 450-500HP RWD cars, how is any Honda going to be much quicker let alone 2 seconds quicker?<P>I'd like to see this, and some time slips to prove me wrong.<P><P>------------------<BR>86 GT fastback 4 speed<BR>85 sport coupe 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000021||crzyone||02-18-2001||12:04 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/455.jpg"> <P>I don't have any time slips on this, but I'm guessing it'll beat your friends Honda.  I'm not trying to start a war, Fieros and Hondas are easily beat by alot of Sports Cars.  I just think there is alot of exageration happening.<P>PEACE I'M OUTA HERE!<P>------------------<BR>86 GT fastback 4 speed<BR>85 sport coupe 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000022||Eric||02-18-2001||12:50 AM||||Here in "Boonyville, USA", I've seen quite a few imports (mostly Hondas) that could,  indeed, hand my ass to me.  I DO appreciate these cars and the work and money that goes into them.  Most of the time I can see them coming from a mile away though.  They not only look the part of a fast car, they sound it too.  Unfortunatly, this Del Sol was not one of those cars.  If it was, I probably wouldn't be questioning the sexuallity of its owner.  The thing was done up like some high school age hooker on prom night.  And the sounds were most likely from a stock non-VTEC Honda motor pumping through a standard issue fart can.  It reved so nice and smooth; I thought it was singing to me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Now I have raced a stock Civic Si.  I am of the opinion that this car has the same motor as the VTEC Del Sol.  I didn't have much of a problem knocking that guy down after he got a jump on me from a light.  But, I'm sorry, it probably doesn't count because we were racing up a hill, and everyone knows when racing up a hill (everything else being almost equal), the car with the torque advantage wins most every time.  <P>Hey crzyone,  my dad and I are building a Cobra replica.  It should run low to mid 12s on street tires, and 0-60 in under 4 seconds, both without the nitrous.  I don't know, maybe I should pay Black88GT's friend a visit in the snake.  What do you think?  <P>There's no way you can have it all with a fwd car.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000023||crzyone||02-18-2001||12:59 AM||||I think he may have engine trouble and not running to his potential if you ever showed up with a Cobra haha.  Those are definitly one of my favorite cars, and yes with todays technology in tires and engines I'd expect a Cobra to get into the 12's.  I have a hard time believing a Honda getting into the 11's though.  Good luck with the Cobra!<P>------------------<BR>86 GT fastback 4 speed<BR>85 sport coupe 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000024||Standard||02-18-2001||01:09 AM||||Well, on the subject of interior room, I had a friend with a CRX.  Said it gave him plenty of space... oh yeah, did I mention he was 6' 10.5"?  ||||reg||1
Z||000025||Eric||02-18-2001||01:13 AM||||The thing will have a "mild" carbed 302 in it.  It should be good for 350 horsepower according to what other people got with identical setups.  With a 100 shot of N2O, the sky's the limit.  And with a 2000 lb car, it may just decide to get airborne.  Numbers and times are a guess right now, but, unklike a 3.4 buildup in a Fiero, I think I can start running my mouth without worrying about backing it up.  Maybe I should go the Viper forum.||||reg||1
Z||000026||Slammed Fiero||02-18-2001||01:15 AM||||Just talked to my friend phil the owner of the shop<P>The motor is a 99 GSR integra motor. He said that the little 127hp VTEC motors are cheap. A GSR motor and Tranny are not. The car last car he did a conversion on cost $9300. That included converting the rear brakes to discs and adding 4 piston wilwoods upfront.<P>There is no way a vtec in a crx will run 13's ...you would have to mod it. His Type R has a turbo and was written up in turbo magazine a while back , they put it against a NOS fed GSR , both cars ran low 13's. His autocross car is an 85 CRX with a 160hp SiR (canadian) VTEC motor , it weighs 2015lbs and runs 14.01 in the 1/4, Phil is a pioneer in honda engine conversions , you can see his name a lot in turbo, He helped develop Eddie Bello's 9 sec street driven turbo porsche (Bellotech in NY)<P>He said if you think his shop is full of sh** feel free to come to the drags or pick up a magazine , or call him. We aren't talking some backyard conversion here, I can't count the number of times his cars have been in Sport compact car or turbo. He is currently putting a Lexus GS430 V8 in a Mr2 for a guy in Texas.<P>His work isn't the usual hack job you see. it's done right. Phone Japenese engine supply in Toronto and inquire about engines and transmissions, I would be glad to get you the phone number so you can see for yourself. Even the older ZC16 motors go for $1000 to $1500<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||Black88GT||02-18-2001||04:20 PM||||Ummm crzyone, maybe in Canada they don't have 11 second Honda's, but here in the States FWD Honda's have been running 11s for a while now.  Pick up ANY Super Street or Sport Compact Car.  I believe the last Super Street had a 9 second Civic Hatchaback on the cover.<P>Mid-Atlantic Motorsports doesn't do hack jobs either.  They did tell my friend they gave him a discount since they knew eachother from way back but it was only a 10% discount.  $9300 is a rip off I don't care who does it.<P>That 455 Fiero, I for one would like to see it make 2 runs without blowing a tranny.  Thats if they used a Fiero tranny.  Also, try taking a hard turn with that 30/70 weight ratio....<P>To reiterate, I am not trying to say that my friends CRX can beat any car in the whole world because Honda's are so great.  I am just saying that, contrary to popular belief, not every Honda is a ricer and you can make them just as fast if not faster then Fiero's.  <P>Keep in mind that these 9 and 10 second Honda's are usually built for one reason: ADVERTISEMENT!  They want to be on the cover of all the import mags so everyone see's their promotional stickers....<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000028||Sleeper||02-18-2001||08:57 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B><P>He said if you think his shop is full of sh** feel free to come to the drags or pick up a magazine<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ok, i went to the drags today, IDRC season opener in palmdale. well before the pros went down the 1/4 mile they were having bracket racing...there was a 88 crx down there that ran a 11.40/125mph, stock vtec motor out of a prelude(195hp or so) with a 70 shot of nos and it was gutted with a fiberglass front end, thats it and oh it had a sticker on the side that said "runs 11's on a bread & butter budget". my friend(crx owner) went and talked to the guy and he said before the nos and fiberglass front clip he was running mid 13's.  your buddy at the shop is over pricing ppl cuz he knows that they haven't heard how cheap the swap is to do, he's just doing what any tuner shop would do: get the most money out of something. <P>my friend has a 90 corrado(VW) its gutted has the stock 1.8 sohc supercharged motor and a 70 shot of nos and he runs low 13's. <P>WHAT IT ALL COMES DOWN TO IS THAT GUTTING YOUR CAR IS THE SAME AS ADDING HORSEPOWER. and thats what import dudes are doing.<P>-----------<P>p.s. why was the 427 cobra brought up in this post? who in their right mind would race a cobra now(authentic or replica) they're worth too much, that was a dumb idea for a car to prove a point. and BLACK88GT i was exactly the same ways so now i like and respect all cars now.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Sleeper (edited 02-18-2001).]||||reg||11
