Z||000036||danny boy||02-19-2001||05:49 PM|||| I'm faster than a Viper 0-60. But I'm staying out of this one....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stealth_feb2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000037||Predator||02-19-2001||07:00 PM|||| I'm not getting into the my car is faster than yours testosterone match here. It's interesting reading this stuff though. I have seen some foreign cars around my area that are extremely fast, and could probably blow my Turbo 2.8 away. I don't race so I will never know. I gave that stupid stuff up after my teen years. I built my car for my tastes, and I really don't care if the funny looking yellow thing beside me is faster or not. I quit the car wars a long time ago when I grew up and realized there will always be someone who can beat you. I realized this before I wrapped my car around a tree trying to find out. I have known several people who have died trying to prove they were faster. There have been several rich kids around here recently who have gotten seriously hurt or killed with their overblown Honda's and other foreign cars that their parents are too stupid to realize a 16 year old can't handle. I have two teens now and would never buy them a car like that. To me building a car that handles well, performs well, and looks good is all you need. Going overboard with a 9 second streetcar is just a stupid waste of money. This is just my opinion. It irritates me when I read these kinds of posts where people bash each other’s cars to prove theirs is better. I have owned several different types of cars, and have been happy with most. Each one having it's advantages, and disadvantages. It doesn't really matter if it is a foreign car or a domestic. If you build the car beyond what it is designed for then you are just building a tomb.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000038||DXR_DAD||02-20-2001||12:43 AM||||There is some confusing info on this thread, just want to clear some of it up.<P>-A CRX weighs about 2,000-2,200lbs.<P>-A Del Sol weighs about 2,300-2,500lbs.<P>-Dropping in a B16A will not get a CRX into the 13's, it should put you into the mid to high 14's.<P>-A motor swap on a honda should not cost you $9,000 unless your getting mods with the motor.<P>-Motor swap prices for Hondas are like this, w/o labor:<P>(160-170HP) B16A/B17A $1,000-$3,000<BR>(170-210HP) B18C1/5 $2,900-$4,500<BR>(190-200HP) H22A $2,900-$3,300<P>expect to pay between $800-$1,200 for labor.<P>-Dropping in a B16A motor into a CRX will not product 13 sec time slips, maybe a B18C1 with slicks.  If traction is not a problem then an H22A will get you into the 13's.<P>-For $10,000 you can make a CRX hit 12's, if the prices are right.<P>-In a straight up race a Del Sol VTEC vs. a 2.8 Fiero would be a good race, but I would have to give it up to the 2.8 Fiero.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000039||RNGCRSH||02-20-2001||12:46 AM||||I know absolutly nothing about imports and racing. But, I was watching motorweek this weekend, and the were showing clips, from some dragrace, that was all imports. They had guys driving to the track then putting fat slicks up front and running 11's in the 1/4 mile. They showed a crx with an integra motor that ran mid 9's. It just looked so damn funny with those big slicks on the front.||||reg||1
Z||000040||GT Bastard||02-20-2001||08:12 AM||||Back up the truck.... A B16A has got 143 hp according to my rice-boy magazine...  That's not far from stock.  No way he's running 13's without forced induction or completely gutting it.  I raced a 99 Civic 2-door with a B16A2 and a turbocharger running 6psi boost.  It could BARELY pull away from my modded 2.8.  After we raced I saw what was under this guys hood and he was for real.  I also talked to the guy who built the car, and it's exactly what the guy said it was.  His excuse was that the car hadn't been tuned yet....   Too bad my rattling(and sometimes smoking) SE will give a turbocharged jap motor a run for it's money. Sheesh...  There's a turbocharged jap motor CRX running mid 12's here, but that car is 100% race-ready.  Roll cage, gutted, lots of boost, slicks, etc...||||reg||1
