Z||000048||Slammed Fiero||02-21-2001||12:24 PM||||You can't wait til one of us gets smoked by a civic CRX with a big motor??<P>How about the 9 million mis guided kids in this world who get beat every second of every day when they pull up next to 5.0ltrs, Camaro's ,vettes, 911's , anything with over 200hp with there riced out cars , decals all over , home lowering jobs , thinking that their K&N filter and cold air intake make them run 13's.<P>There are a lot of fast crx's and civis out there/ I have friends who would kill me in the 1/4 with their hondas's , but they represent such a small fraction of whats really on the road. I was coming back from an Autocross in Ottawa this summer when a Kid in a Type R tried to race the 417hp 911 I was riding in ..... GO HOME!<P>Now someone is going to post ..if he had a turbo and a intercooler and was running NOS he could kick your ass...Yes tons of money later he could go faster , yipeee.<P>Anyone remember the article in HOTROD ?? 10 Sec's for 10 grand?? I will go get a old nova , follow that article word for word and there's not a street driven honda that could touch me.  Once more I run on pump gas , my motor is as basic as it gets , if I break anything I can find dozens more parts in the wrecking yard. It may not be stlyish , but you can go get any civic with your BA_XYZ motors and I will beat you like a rented mule.<BR> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.riceboypage.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.riceboypage.com/</A> <P>Go here ,he explains it pretty well, and hopefully this will end it all. This guy has the best view on the who riceboy syndrom I have ever seen , a lot of you quoting engine combo's in cars should go read this.<P><BR>There is a guy floating around the net with a 12 sec Chrysler 4 cyl minivan it runs a 2.2 turbo motor , it was featured in Grass Roots motorsports. Anything can be made to go fast.. Can you imagine the face of a 13 Sec CRX getting his ass whipped by a minivan??<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000049||MEC91Firebird||02-21-2001||01:44 PM||||Im actually kinda suprised by FWD cars.  Ive only ever had one daily driver RWD car, My 91 firebird!!  yeah, but as far as FWD cars go, when my 88 voyager died, my parents leased a 98 Corolla, and ill tell you from experince, for a FWD!!!!  wow, that thing will go!  handles better than my F-body, comparable to a fiero, I can surly see why the corolla has been used as a world rally car.  As far as power, there is like nothing after you go of the line, but you launch from the line like a rocket.  I also drive a Chrysler LHS, which is a FWD V-6, and with traction control off, it will spin the tires off the line and it has some nice power in every situation.   Intrestingly enough, I like the FWD cars when im just driving around and taking off from the stop lights, but the RWD's are alot more fun driving around curvy mountain roads.  (I must be like the ricers in one of the new car mags Automobile i think that like to slide around the corners)<P>Just my opinions and rambalings||||reg||6
