Z||000052||Sleeper||02-22-2001||09:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>You can't wait til one of us gets smoked by a civic CRX with a big motor??<P>How about the 9 million mis guided kids in this world who get beat every second of every day when they pull up next to 5.0ltrs, Camaro's ,vettes, 911's , anything with over 200hp with there riced out cars , decals all over , home lowering jobs , thinking that their K&N filter and cold air intake make them run 13's.<P>There are a lot of fast crx's and civis out there/ I have friends who would kill me in the 1/4 with their hondas's , but they represent such a small fraction of whats really on the road. I was coming back from an Autocross in Ottawa this summer when a Kid in a Type R tried to race the 417hp 911 I was riding in ..... GO HOME!<P>Now someone is going to post ..if he had a turbo and a intercooler and was running NOS he could kick your ass...Yes tons of money later he could go faster , yipeee.<P>Anyone remember the article in HOTROD ?? 10 Sec's for 10 grand?? I will go get a old nova , follow that article word for word and there's not a street driven honda that could touch me.  Once more I run on pump gas , my motor is as basic as it gets , if I break anything I can find dozens more parts in the wrecking yard. It may not be stlyish , but you can go get any civic with your BA_XYZ motors and I will beat you like a rented mule.<BR> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.riceboypage.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.riceboypage.com/</A> <P>Go here ,he explains it pretty well, and hopefully this will end it all. This guy has the best view on the who riceboy syndrom I have ever seen , a lot of you quoting engine combo's in cars should go read this.<P><BR>There is a guy floating around the net with a 12 sec Chrysler 4 cyl minivan it runs a 2.2 turbo motor , it was featured in Grass Roots motorsports. Anything can be made to go fast.. Can you imagine the face of a 13 Sec CRX getting his ass whipped by a minivan??<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>boy, that was pretty DEEP man.<P>why is your pricing always off? please dude, i didn't read that article "10sec for 10 grand" so i waited to post(cuz i don't believe it) so i could ask one of my friends and his dad if they read it, but they didn't. so thinking that the title says it all i asked them if its true "10 sec for 10 grand?" AND THEY LAUGHED AT ME. cuz it don't, ya know? my friend knows this one guy from other friends-he has a 70 chevelle with a professionally built 355 that runs high tens all day long at the track(i can get the engine specs if you want them?) and he's only put like $6500 into it. my friend across the street has a 67 nova with a 383 that he built himself and he ran it once 12.55/132mph with a shitty 1 sec reaction time, and he has a little over $5000 into the motor. is it really gonna take another 5 grand for him to bust into the 10's? i don't think so. sometimes i think ppl lose some hope when they read an article in a mag and the price is way blown out of proportion and i interstand the HOT ROD is a dope mag but their probably going to one shop out of many that will do it for a lot less. that brings up something else i've read on here that ppl say it costs 4 to 5 grand for a 3.8 conversion in their fiero. that is another ridiclous price for a simple engine swap. maybe you need HOOK-UPS from ppl your cool with but that may be just me cuz prices just seem to be blown up here.<P>riceboypage.com is cool....heres another <A HREF="http://www.beaterz.com" TARGET=_blank>www.beaterz.com</A>  its pretty funny too.||||reg||11
Z||000053||Slammed Fiero||02-22-2001||10:59 PM||||I'm just quoting the hot rod artice, it says plainly on the cover  "10 seconds for 10 grand" It outlines everything about the Nova. I will scan the article as soon as I get a chance.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000054||Slammed Fiero||02-22-2001||11:05 PM||||I have never looked into building a 10 sec straight line car , just quoting the magazine. IF it's cheaper than 10 grand you prove my point even better. The article was 10 grand including the rust free nova , not just the motor. I think 4- 5 grand for a 3.8 SC conversion is believeable. <P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000055||Black88GT||02-22-2001||11:59 PM||||They stopped making CRX's in '91, and the B16A they swap in is the same motor found in Civic Si's 1999-2000, not sure what if anything else uses the motor.  The other day I ran into a modded CRX in the parking lot, looked modded so I strike up a conversation with the guy.  Come to find out, he has an Integra Type R motor in his CRX.  I think its called the B18C1 or something like that.  But he did his whole project himself and it was all under 11 grand when he was done.  He tweaked the motor so its about 230 Hp he estimated, and he took out some of the interior (not "gutted" since he drives it more then just at the track), and he has an intake/header and exhaust.  Showed me high 11 second time slips with slicks.  I didn't want to race him after I saw them!  He did say he was looking into getting an EIP sponsorship because they have FWD imports running 8s and 9s.  Also the car handles so sweet.  Take an outdated muscle car and run 10s or whatever is great but your stuck with a car that can't make a turn with its solid rear axle and gross weight of a small country.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||12
Z||000056||Slammed Fiero||02-23-2001||10:08 AM||||I more than anyone like cars that handle. But lets take 2 strip cars. A nova and a honda , Both Running 10's. Which car do you think is more streetable at a 10 sec level. In a rear drive application a nova can run a 10" DOT slick and turn 10's. a 10 sec Civic or honda needs to be fully gutted and have huge ass slicks up front to get into the 10's. There goes any handling the Honda once possessed. or streetability..how many 10, 11 sec street chevies do you see, actually running in 10 sec trim on the streets? I can go to the local hangout on friday saturday night and there will be lots of them. <P>This is just a question , no need to flame me , But High 11's with only 230hp??? No NOS??<P><BR>Here's why I ask the question...<P>Straight from superstreet<P>88 Civic Si , no interior , 1.6ltr motor with mods a mile long (I won't type them out) , Turbo'd , spearco intercooler 280hp , 238Ft lbs torque ..dynoed , runs mid 12's on slicks.... My 89 Civic weighed in @ 2100lbs.. Just as light as any 2nd gen Crx , and about 200lbs or so heavier than a 1st generation. I have seena  lot of Honda's weighed at autocrosses..Gutted out ones<P>There are about 10 more cars in this magazine wit the same combo running mid to hi 12's , Guys in the 11's have 400hp<P>Here's another example .Turbo Magazine<P>11.835 sec 1/4 mile Del Sol. B16 motor , running a T350G turbo @21 psi boost , intercooler....No HP level given but this thing looks mean , no interior and big ass slicks (again so much for handling) I bet it has a bit more than 230hp.<P>Ok so I'm getting a bit anal about this , But that guys CRX doesn't add up. I can pick up some 11 sec time slips at the drags too and say their mine , but with only 230hp on Tap , it doesn't add up.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
