Z||000068||Predator||02-25-2001||01:12 PM||||This post could go on forever. I think one point everyone needs to get back to is everyone so far has been comparing one modified car to another. Also there is a big tech difference between 1985 - 1988 to a new car. I would hope that any high performance new car could beat a comparable car built in 1985. If you want to compare cars for real compare a stock 1985 - 1988 Fiero to a car in that time frame. This constant comparison of built cars to the Fiero's is kind of stupid. It does not matter what kind of car it is you can build it to go fast for enough money so this whole thread is pointless. I like a lot more about my Fiero than the fact that it can go fast. It is a matter of preference. It really does not matter that a new foreign car can outrun mine. It should outrun mine. A car built for performance now a days has a big advantage in technology over a car design in the early 80's. For every fast Foreign car there is a faster domestic, and visa versa. We are all here on the forum to help each other with a common reason. We enjoy our Fiero's. I am not a Fiero fanatic, but I really like working on my car. It's a hobby. It does not matter that some kid down the street has a Honda that can outrun mine. I care enough about my car not to abuse it trying to find out. I want to enjoy my Fiero for years down the road, and not blow it up or total it out trying to prove a point that mine is faster than his. If you bought your Fiero just to outrun everybody on the street then that's your prerogative, but I bought mine, because I enjoy driving it. I put the turbo kit on it for a kick in the pants, and not to go around challenging everyone to a race. To each his own, and this is just my opinion. It just bothers me reading through this how everybody keeps aging the other on even though neither is really right or wrong. It's the old thing about keeping up with the Jones’s. You build your motor faster then mine then I mod mine more and so forth. If you guys got the kind of money to keep building up your cars to beat the other guy then more power to you. When I first started coming to this forum it was one guy helping another, and that was it. Lately I have seen more of these threads where it is just a match to see who's is bigger. It's kind of sad in a way. I think I will quit coming here for a while, and maybe it will eventually get back to what this forum was originally started for. Sorry for the ranting. When I get this upset over a thread I am definitely coming here way too much. See you guys around. Predator out. ||||reg||1
Z||000069||Sleeper||02-25-2001||02:02 PM||||oh my god. whats up dude? this post started out as Eric saying a gay FRUITY(i liked that word he used) ricer boy was just plain acting gay in his little bi*ch car del sol. then Black88GT stated that he knows someone with a b16 in crx and it runs 13's and i agreed with him and some ppl didn't. thats all what this post is about, man. we're not knocking each others car saying "my car is faster than yours, neener-neener-neerner" you can build any car to go fast. this is just a little argument about b16 motors in a crx running 13's and a guess some other cars too but its not like i'm gonna see Slammed Fiero on another post and be like fu*kyou just cuz we didn't agree on this post, come-on dude this is OT Section. ppl don't have to be this sentsitive.   <P>hugh-- i'm getting my friends mixed up, my friends nova ran a 12.55/115mph...132mph was my other friends corrado et was 11.40. though i still don't understand the elasped time thingy, i may sound retarded but drag racing to me is rolling up to the line and waiting for the green light to appear and boom there you go, hopefully you have a better reaction time cuz then your in-favor of getting a better et and winning the race.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Sleeper (edited 02-25-2001).]||||reg||1
